after the on tante victory in the First  World War Germany lost this territory  which notably included what's called the  Polish corridor this area was handed  over to the newly founded polish  Republic in order to grant Poland access  to the sea and thus control over its  international trade this corridor lacked  any major ports barring one which was  located in the city of Danzig known as  Gdansk in Polish the city in the  surrounding area was overwhelmingly  German and so it wasn't directly awarded  to Poland but instead was made an  independent state but of course given  its geopolitical position it's special  status and the conflict surrounding it  the question should be asked how free  was the free city of Danzig well there  were many ways in which it acted as any  other free nation could it had its own  currency the Danzig golden and for the  most part it could set its own fiscal  policy although you should know that  Danzig nearly always struggled  financially the free city had its own  Parliament the Volk star which was  elected by any one man a woman over the  age of 20 it issued its own passports  and his citizens were neither Germans  nor poles but was simply danziger's the  dancy constitution made sure that all  people who lived in the city were to be  treated equal in all respects but German  Polish M&amp;T remained high throughout the  period of the Free Cities existence part  of this was of course due to the war but  also that throughout the other areas of  Germany which were incorporated into  Poland the Germans who remained there  faced major discrimination so since  Danzig was the largest port in the  Polish corridor the majority of Polish  exports traveled through it  Poland wanted to maintain trade  independence and so the League of  Nations gave Poland the right to  determine what went in and out of the  port and it was Poland not Danzig that  could set tariffs on goods now the free  city did get a proportion of this income  or when polish german relations soured a  trade war per account thus the  danziger's who wanted to join germany  were forced to implement tariffs against  it which really soured the relations  between itself and Poland Danzig didn't  have its own military which meant that  when Poland decided to send over 150  troops there to make a point to the  newly elected German Chancellor the  people could do nothing about it  these tensions combined with the desire  to be reunited with Germany make it  unsurprising that throughout the 1930s  the people of Danzig voted the Nazi  Party into power there the free city of  Danzig come to an end after the German  invasion of Poland where it was brought  back into Germany and after the  conclusion of the Second World War it  was made a permanent part of Poland the  city was supposed to be a sovereign  independent state but this frankly  couldn't happen  whilst Poland needed access to  international overseas trade the city  could never  truly be free and whilst the people of  the city were overwhelmingly German and  wish to remain so it had to be free  this combined with Germany proper  wanting it back meant the conflict was  always going to erupt over the city's  future I hope you enjoyed this episode  and thank you for watching with extra  thanks to my patrons that you see on  screen now and a special thanks to James  Bissonnette David archaeologist zarqa  flash party boy Co Rob Waterhouse Yashar  Enderman Chris wicker Myles Bailey Brent  guard Michael Reynolds Gustav Swann tune  Ric onion duck  Maggie packs Kowski Winston K word for  Celia vadas Anthony Beckett Adam Harvey  Ike Skye Chappell and the amusement park  Ives
 

